  "claim": "The animated Disney film, in which Arthur Gould-Porter played the part of Captain Greer, not The Journey of Natty Gann, is a British-influenced film.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bedknobs and Broomsticks. Sentence: Bedknobs and Broomsticks is a 1971 British-American musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions and released by Buena Vista Distribution Company in North America on December 13, 1971.\nPage: The Journey of Natty Gann. Sentence: The Journey of Natty Gann is a 1985 American film directed by Jeremy Paul Kagan, produced by Walt Disney Pictures and released by Buena Vista Distribution.\nPage: Arthur Gould-Porter. Sentence: His film and television career spanned from 1942 to 1977, and although mainly a character actor he is remembered for his part as Captain Greer in Disney's \"Bedknobs and Broomsticks\" and for his reoccurring role as Ravenswood the butler in \"The Beverley Hillbillies\".",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Bedknobs and Broomsticks. Sentence: Bedknobs and Broomsticks is a 1971 British-American musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions and released by Buena Vista Distribution Company in North America on December 13, 1971.\nPage: The Journey of Natty Gann. Sentence: The Journey of Natty Gann is a 1985 American film directed by Jeremy Paul Kagan, produced by Walt Disney Pictures and released by Buena Vista Distribution.\nPage: Arthur Gould-Porter. Sentence: His film and television career spanned from 1942 to 1977, and although mainly a character actor he is remembered for his part as Captain Greer in Disney's \"Bedknobs and Broomsticks\" and for his reoccurring role as Ravenswood the butler in \"The Beverley Hillbillies\".",
